## Bus factor: `lib/index.js`

**Reviewer: Troy Goode.** He is the only active deep owner.

| Author | Commits | Share | Last touch |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 29 | 47% | 2026-04-10 (active) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 4 | 6% | 2017-10 (inactive) |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 4 | 6% | 2015-05 (inactive) |
| Simon Mansfield | 3 | 5% | 2013-05 (inactive) |
| 21 others | 1–2 each | about 35% | all inactive since 2021 or earlier |

- **File bus factor:** 25 authors have touched it in 62 non-merge commits. No one owns more than 80% of it, so it is not single-owner by the usual threshold. In practice it is 1, because only Troy Goode has committed in the last year. The one other recent author, Fiona Formatter, made the 2026-04-12 reformat commit (`62628c0`), which was a style-only change.
- **Dependents:** 238 lines. `package.json` and 5 test files (`test/test.js`, `test/vary.js`, `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/issue-2.js`) reference it. It is the package entry point, so every consumer depends on it.
- **Risk:** MEDIUM. Ownership is spread across many people, but nearly all of them have left. One person holds the working knowledge, and the file is the main entry point.

### Recommendations
1. **Immediate:** Ask Troy Goode to review. Also get a second reviewer who has not touched the file, so the knowledge spreads.
2. **Before merging:** Run the 5 test files above. They are the only direct coverage.
3. **Blame context:** Run `/project-pilot:history lib/index.js` for the section you are changing. Some past fixes may encode non-obvious behavior, such as the Safari pre-flight workaround (`d3304ab`) and the `maxAge: 0` fix (`01477dc`).

